WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.330
Pour a glass of fizzy water.

2
00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:06.530
Tiny bubbles stream
upwards, one after another.

3
00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:09.750
Now deal out six number
cards, in a muddle.

4
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:13.970
A computer can put them in order
using a method called a bubble sort.

5
00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:17.130
But nothing here fizzes,
and nothing floats.

6
00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:20.270
So what can number cards
have to do with bubbles?

7
00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:23.470
In this mission, you'll
compare an adjacent pair:

8
00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:27.010
two neighbouring cards, starting
at the front of the list.

9
00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:30.050
If the pair is in the
wrong order, you swap them.

10
00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:33.670
Then you move along one place
and compare the next pair.

11
00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:37.520
Your mission: explain where the
bubbles are hiding in this sort.
